Cmn1=MODULE NAME: CH Audio Dist. SYSTEM Device Start and Stop v2.1 (cm)\\
Cmn2=\\CATEGORY: CrestronHome\\\\MODULE VERSION: 2.1.01 (04/04/2005)\\
Cmn3=\\CRESTRONHOME PACKAGE VERSION: 2.0\\\\SUMMARY: Sends generic "start,"||1
Cmn4="stop," "on," and "off" commands to sources based on usage.\\\\MODULE||1
Cmn5=DESCRIPTION:\\This module is designed for use with the CrestronHome||1
Cmn6=module package. It monitors the\\sources that are currently being||1
Cmn7=accessed for use by up to 32 rooms, and sends a generic\\start,||1
Cmn8=stop, on, and off commands to these sources based on usage. For||1
Cmn9=example, if a source\\is selected by a room and no other rooms had||1
Cmn10=been listening to that source, an on command\\may be issued if this||1
Cmn11=device had been unused long enough. This command would be followed||1
Cmn12=by\\a "start" command, which might be "PLAY" if the device were||1
Cmn13=a CD player. When a source\\becomes unused (by rooms turning off||1
Cmn14=or changing sources), a "stop" command is issued. If a\\source remains||1
Cmn15=unused for long enough, an "off" command is issued.\\\\Note that||1
Cmn16=to make use of the on and off commands, you might need to include||1
Cmn17=some sort of\\power sensing, such as current-sensing or video-sensing.
Cmn18=||1If a source has discreet on and off\\power commands, then a sensor||1
Cmn19=is not necessary.\\\\INPUT DESCRIPTIONS: \\\\Name             Type||1
Cmn20=Description\\---------------------------------\\room_x_source||3
Cmn21=||3A  The input currently routed to room x on the CNX-PAD8/PAD8A/BIPAD8.
Cmn22=||1Connect this \\                      signal from the output of||1
Cmn23=the CrestronHome Room Control module.\\\\\\OUTPUT DESCRIPTIONS:||1
Cmn24=\\\\Name             Type Description\\-------------------------
Cmn25=--------\\source_x_start    D   A signal that will pulse one second||1
Cmn26=after a source that had previously been\\                      "stopped"||1
Cmn27=is selected. The one second delay is to allow the device to power\\
Cmn28=||Fon, in case it had been powered off previously.
Cmn29=||1This signal would typically\\                      be connected||1
Cmn30=to a "play" function for transport devices, like CD players.\\||2
Cmn31=||DIf a given source does not require a start command||1
Cmn32=(e.g. Tuner), then leave\\                      this signal unconnected.
Cmn33=\\source_x_stop     D   A signal that will pulse whenever a source||1
Cmn34=has remained unused for the amount\\                      of time||1
Cmn35=specified by the "device stop delay" parameter. See the PARAMETER\\
Cmn36=||FDESCRIPTIONS section below for more details.
Cmn37=||1This signal would typically\\                      be connected||1
Cmn38=to a "stop" function for transport devices, like CD players.\\||2
Cmn39=||DIf a given source does not require a stop command||1
Cmn40=(e.g. Tuner), then leave\\                      this signal unconnected.
Cmn41=\\source_x_on       D   A signal that will pulse whenever a source||1
Cmn42=that had been previously turned\\                      off is selected.
Cmn43=||1If it is desired to shut a source on and off based on usage,\\||1
Cmn44=||Econnect this signal to the "power off" command||1
Cmn45=for the source. If the source\\                      has only a||1
Cmn46="toggling" power control, then you should use some sort of power-
Cmn47=\\                      sensing device such as the ST-CS (current||1
Cmn48=sensor), or ST-VS (video sensor), \\                      in conjunction||1
Cmn49=with the "Current Sense Logic" module (note that this module\\||2
Cmn50=||Dworks with current- or video- sensors). If a||1
Cmn51=source has no remote power\\                      control at all,||1
Cmn52=then you can use a switched AC controller such as the ST-PC\\||3
Cmn53=||Cto turn the power on and off, if desired.\\source_x_off||1
Cmn54=||5D   A signal that will pulse whenever a source has remained||1
Cmn55=unused for the amount\\                      of time specified by||1
Cmn56=the "device off delay" parameter. See the PARAMETER\\||;
Cmn57=||;DESCRIPTIONS section below for more details. For details||1
Cmn58=on what to connect\\                      this signal to, see the||1
Cmn59=description of the "source_x_on" signal.\\source_x_usage    A||3
Cmn60=An analog signal that contains the current number of "rooms" that||1
Cmn61=are currently\\                      using source "x". These outputs||1
Cmn62=should be connected to the "Room Control with\\||A
Cmn63=||5MultiSource" module, to decide which MultiSource input to select.
Cmn64=\\\\PARAMETER DESCRIPTIONS: \\\\Name                 Type     Description\\
Cmn65=-----------------------------------------\\"device stop delay"||2
Cmn66=TIME     Specifies the delay time from when a device is no longer||1
Cmn67=in use, to when\\                              a stop command is||1
Cmn68=actually issued.\\"device off delay"   TIME     Specifies the delay||1
Cmn69=time from when a device is no longer in use, to when\\||:
Cmn70=||Dan off command is actually issued. Although||1
Cmn71=it is not enforced, this time\\                              should||1
Cmn72=be set to a longer value than the "device stop delay."\\\\OPS USED||1
Cmn73=FOR TESTING: 5.04.10x\\\\COMPILER USED FOR TESTING: 1.00.28\\\\SAMPLE||1
Cmn74=PROGRAM: CrestronHome demo\\\\REVISION HISTORY: \\\\v1.0: Initial||1
Cmn75=release\\\\v2.0: -Uses digital outputs instead of an encoded serial||1
Cmn76=output.\\      -Added on and off output signals\\      -Added "source_x_usage"||1
Cmn77=outputs for use by the "Room Control with MultiSource" modules\\
Cmn78=\\v2.1: - Supports 24 sources\\\\v2.1.01: - Fixed bug that caused||1
Cmn79=source_{N}_on signals to go high on startup.
]
